<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>OpenVSA.Synthesis</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyTitle>OpenVSA.Synthesis</AssemblyTitle>
    <Description>The synthetic modulated source of REQ-SIM-001 and the controllable impairments of REQ-SIM-002: modulation formats, pulse shaping, bursts and the measurements that read an impairment back out of the samples.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Core alone, and that is the whole point of this assembly existing.

    A generator that referenced the demodulator could not be used by OpenVSA.Hal.Sim without putting
    an L3 analysis assembly underneath an L0 transport; a generator that lived with the bench
    harness could not be used by the analysis stack's own tests, because the harness references the
    VISA transport and REQ-ARC-001 requires that stack to build with no transport present. It had
    lived with the harness, and that is exactly how it turned main red.

    So: samples in, samples out, and nothing about how they are analysed. The one thing that did
    reach into OpenVSA.Demod, turning a burst's own truth into a SymbolTrace, stayed behind in
    the harness as an extension, because converting a generator's truth into a demodulator's result
    type is an analysis-side convenience rather than part of generating anything.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\OpenVSA.Core\OpenVSA.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
